course: dictionary
lesson: 13137
title: Forceful and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Forceful is an adjective. It describes someone or something that is strong, confident or powerful. «Mia gave a forceful speech, and the whole class turned to listen.» Mia is not shouting. Her strong, confident words make people pay attention.
explain: The word can also mean using strength or force. «The wind gave a forceful push, and the gate swung wide.» The push is powerful, so the gate moves with force. Ask yourself: is this a person being strong and confident, or something using real power? The sentence will tell you.
explain: In stories, a forceful character may be bossy or determined. «Aunt Rosa has a forceful personality, so everyone does what she says.» Being forceful is different from being assertive. Assertive means stating your view politely and calmly.
fact: Forceful is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as a person, a voice, a kick or an argument.
fact: «A forceful argument» means a strong, convincing argument that makes people listen.
fact: «A forceful kick» in sport uses lots of power.
fact: Forceful is not the same as assertive: assertive means speaking up for yourself in a polite, calm way.
exercise: «Mia gave a forceful speech, and the whole class turned to listen.» What does forceful mean here? | Lost and confused | *Strong and confident, so people listen | Quiet and shy | Tired and sleepy
exercise: «The wind gave a forceful push, and the gate swung wide.» What does forceful suggest? | Very gentle and slow | *Using great strength or power | Pretty and bright | Very cold
exercise: «The captain's forceful kick sent the ball over the fence.» Find and copy the adjective in this sentence. | kick | *forceful | sent | captain
test: Which word is closest in meaning to forceful? | Lazy | Gentle | *Powerful | Silent
test: Tom says forceful means the same as polite. Why is he wrong? | Forceful is a noun | *Forceful can mean bossy, while assertive is the polite, calm way to speak up | Forceful means very quiet | Forceful and polite mean exactly the same
exam: Which sentence uses forceful correctly? | We forceful ate our lunch in the park. | Forceful the book is on the table. | *The forceful wind knocked over the bins. | The sleepy cat yawned forceful on the mat.
